 STT treats store-to-load forwarding as an implicit branch on the load's address and delays resolving it until that address is untainted~\cite[\S 6.4.2]{yu2019stt}. ReCon's implementation of STT~\cite{recon} checks a load's taint only on its cache path: when an older in-flight store has the same address, the load takes the store's data and completes without passing the taint check (\texttt{lsq\_unit.cc:2019}). Its completion time therefore reveals whether its secret-derived address matches the store's. Fig.~\ref{fig:reconstl} shows this in generated test inst-014536. 
